":"The starting position of the Fantasy main line. Engines think White is slightly better, but Stjepan likes Black: White's pawns are overextended, the diagonal towards his king is weak if he doesn't castle soon, and the center is easy to undermine until White is left with hanging pawns.","ts":1204}]}]}],"comment":"Pinning the knight.","ts":1196},{"id":"n8","san":"exd4","uci":"e5d4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp3ppp/2p5/8/3pP3/5N2/PPP3PP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 0 6","children":[]},{"id":"n9","san":"Be6","uci":"c8e6","fen":"rn1qkbnr/pp3ppp/2p1b3/4p3/3PP3/5N2/PPP3PP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 2 6","children":[]},{"id":"n10","san":"Nf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp3ppp/2p2n2/4p3/3PP3/5N2/PPP3PP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 2 6","children":[]}]}],"comment":"The only active move: strike in the center and disrupt White's idea immediately.","ts":1188}]}]},{"id":"n11","san":"e6","uci":"e7e6","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp3ppp/2p1p3/3p4/3PP3/5P2/PPP3PP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 4","children":[],"comment":"The more passive way: e6 just solidifies. The downside is that White never has to take on d5, so the bishop on c8 is stuck like in the French. Here, take on e4.","ts":1237},{"id":"n12","san":"Qb6","uci":"d8b6","fen":"rnb1kbnr/pp2pppp/1qp5/3p4/3PP3/5P2/PPP3PP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 1 4","children":[]},{"id":"n13","san":"g6","uci":"g7g6","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pp1p/2p3p1/3p4/3PP3/5P2/PPP3PP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 4","children":[]},{"id":"n14","san":"a6","uci":"a7a6","fen":"rnbqkbnr/1p2pppp/p1p5/3p4/3PP3/5P2/PPP3PP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 4","children":[]}],"intro":"The third most popular reply to d5 is f3, the Fantasy Variation (also called the Tartakower). White reinforces e4 with a pawn and asks Black to take, so he can recapture towards the center.","introTs":1155,"leadIn":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1"},{"san":"c6","uci":"c7c6","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2p5/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2"},{"san":"d4","uci":"d2d4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2p5/8/3PP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR b 