2n5/3p4/2PP4/8/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 1 5","children":[]}],"comment":"The Panov, or Panov-Botvinnik, Attack: one of the most aggressive ways to fight the Caro-Kann, and a favorite of strong players. White accepts an isolated queen's pawn, but in return Black has nothing left in the center and White gets a lot of piece activity.","ts":1368},{"id":"n13","san":"Bd3","uci":"f1d3","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/8/3p4/3P4/3B4/PPP2PPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 1 4","children":[{"id":"n14","san":"Nc6","uci":"b8c6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pp2pppp/2n5/3p4/3P4/3B4/PPP2PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 2 5","children":[{"id":"n15","san":"c3","uci":"c2c3","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pp2pppp/2n5/3p4/3P4/2PB4/PP3PPP/RNBQK1NR b KQkq - 0 5","children":[{"id":"n16","san":"Nf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"r1bqkb1r/pp2pppp/2n2n2/3p4/3P4/2PB4/PP3PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 1 6","children":[],"comment":"Black puts the knight on f6 and develops normally.","ts":1335},{"id":"n17","san":"e5","uci":"e7e5","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pp3ppp/2n5/3pp3/3P4/2PB4/PP3PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 0 6","children":[]},{"id":"n18","san":"Qc7","uci":"d8c7","fen":"r1b1kbnr/ppq1pppp/2n5/3p4/3P4/2PB4/PP3PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 1 6","children":[]},{"id":"n19","san":"g6","uci":"g7g6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pp2pp1p/2n3p1/3p4/3P4/2PB4/PP3PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 0 6","children":[]},{"id":"n20","san":"e6","uci":"e7e6","fen":"r1bqkbnr/pp3ppp/2n1p3/3p4/3P4/2PB4/PP3PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 0 6","children":[]}]}]},{"id":"n21","san":"Nf6","uci":"g8f6","fen":"rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/5n2/3p4/3P4/3B4/PPP2PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 2 5","children":[]},{"id":"n22","san":"e6","uci":"e7e6","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp3ppp/4p3/3p4/3P4/3B4/PPP2PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 0 5","children":[]},{"id":"n23","san":"a6","uci":"a7a6","fen":"rnbqkbnr/1p2pppp/p7/3p4/3P4/3B4/PPP2PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 0 5","children":[]},{"id":"n24","san":"g6","uci":"g7g6","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pp1p/6p1/3p4/3P4/3B4/PPP2PPP/RNBQK1NR w KQkq - 0 5","children":[]}],"comment":"Fischer's way: simply develop with Bd3, castle kingside, put the knight on d2 and play c3. Slightly passive, but it gives White chances.","ts":1311}]}],"intro":"The Exchange Variation: White trades the central pawns, simplifies, and argues that his extra tempo is enough for a favorable position.","introTs":1286,"leadIn":[{"san":"e4","uci":"e2e4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 1"},{"san":"c6","uci":"c7c6","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2p5/8/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 2"},{"san":"d4","uci":"d2d4","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2p5/8/3PP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 2"},{"san":"d5","uci":"d7d5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/3p4/3PP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 3"},{"san":"exd5","uci":"e4d5","fen":"rnbqkbnr/pp2pppp/2p5/3P4/3P4/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 3"}]}]}